    "bio": "Kamindu Mendis is a Sri Lankan all-rounder known for his unique ambidextrous bowling, capable of delivering both slow left-arm orthodox and right-arm off-break. He made his Test debut on July 8, 2022, against Australia, scoring a maiden fifty. In March 2024, he became the first batter in Test history to score centuries in both innings of a match while batting at number 7 or lower. Mendis also holds the world record for scoring fifty-plus in each of his first eight Test matches."
